\section{Failures, limitations, and unsupported claims}
\begin{itemize}
\item This is short-horizon, single-site surface-layer evidence. It does not establish
vertical-profile accuracy, long-range propagation performance, causality, deployment
safety, seasonal generalization, or cross-instrument equivalence.
\item Adjacent atmospheric observations remain correlated even after blocked splitting;
the moving-block bootstrap reduces but cannot eliminate this limitation.
\item Two seeds give a first stability check, not a complete distribution over training
randomness.
\item Calibration on MLO development data is descriptive because that same held-out
block estimates the scale factor. The USNA test, when released, is the independent
confirmatory calibration assessment.
\item Integrated optical metrics and layer behavior are unsupported by a surface-point
task and are marked unsupported rather than reported as zero.
\end{itemize}

